The Opening of the Khmer Art Exhibition in Moscow
On 2 November 2023 at 17:00 (Moscow time) at the Eastern State Museum, Moscow, His Excellency Ambassador of Cambodia PichKhun Panha, accompanied by his Spouse and all officials of the Embassy of Cambodia to the Federation of Russia, participated in the opening ceremony of the exhibition under the theme " In the Shadow of the Angkor Temples
Art of Cambodia", co-organized by the Russian Ministry of Culture and the State Museum of Oriental Art of the Russian Federation
The purpose of this exhibition is to celebrate the 70 th anniversary of the 9 th November Independence Day of the Kingdom of Cambodia
Art of Cambodia" is the first large-scale exhibition dedicated to Khmer art in the last 20 years in the Russian Federation
Through this exhibition, the State Museum of Oriental Art showcases the diversity of traditional Khmer arts and crafts that have been left behind for generations, with more than 150 artifacts related to the magnificent Angkor temples and rich cultural treasures
