The fair is the largest annual tourism event in Serbia with 400 exhibitors from 27 different countries including Cambodia
Farewell to Secretary-General of the United Nations
On 22 February 2024, Ambassador EAT Sophea, Permanent Representative of Cambodia to the United Nations, bid farewell to His Excellency António Guterres, Secretary-General of the United Nations, as her tour of duty has been concluded
Taking this opportunity, Ambassador Sophea affirmed Cambodia's support for the Secretary-General's 2024 priorities to fulfill the people's aspiration for peace, with security and dignity
She also highlighted Cambodia's commitment to further promote cooperation with the United Nations to achieve the sustainable development goals and maintenance of international peace
She also stressed the importance of strengthening rules-based multilateralism to address current global challenges
On 27 February 2024, Madam ROS Ratana, Spouse of the Ambassador of Cambodia to the Republic of Türkiye, hosted the ASEAN Ladies' Circle's (ALC) Gathering 2024 in Ankara
During the event, the Spouse of the Ambassador demonstrated Khmer food "Amok" cooking, and Cambodian tourism promotional video was also shown accordingly
Paying a Courtesy Call on Chairman of Türkiye- Cambodia Inter-Parliamentary Friendship Group of the Grand National Assembly of Türkiye (GNAT)
