On December 5, 2024, at the United Nations Headquarters in New York, His Excellency KEO Chhea presented his credentials to His Excellency António Guterres, Secretary-General of the United Nations, as the Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary and Permanent Representative of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the United Nations
During the meeting, Ambassador KEO Chhea highlighted the Royal Government of Cambodia's priorities in fostering national development and reaffirmed Cambodia's steadfast commitment to strengthening cooperation with the United Nations
He highlights Cambodia’s leadership in global mine action, emphasizing the success of the Fifth Review Conference on the Ottawa Convention, organized under the theme of the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit on a Mine-Free World
On the afternoon of 16th December 2024, Her Excellency RATH Many, Ambassador of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the Republic of India, had a meeting with His Excellency Ashish Kumar Sinha (Joint Secretary South), in charge of Cambodia and other countries in Southeast Asia, at the Ministry of External Affairs of India
During the meeting both sides have discussed on the cooperation to further promote the existing good relations between Cambodia and India to the new heights
The Cambodia-Türkiye Business Forum
On December 12, 2024, the Royal Embassy of Cambodia to the Republic of Türkiye coordinated the Cambodia-Türkiye Business Forum, which was held at the Ankara Chamber of Industry (ASO) in Ankara, Republic of Türkiye, with approximately 50 participants, including representatives from 18 Turkish and 6 Cambodian companies
The business forum was organized to provide the opportunity for Cambodian and Turkish businessmen to discuss the potentials of trade and investment between the two countries, and to explore opportunities for partnerships in investment and business
At the forum, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Ankara Chamber of Industry also signed a Memorandum of Understanding to strengthen cooperation between the two institutions in promoting trade and investment
Taking that opportunity, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce delegation also visited the 1st Organized Industrial Zone in Ankara and studied the operations of four factories, including a furniture factory, an excavator installation factory, a frozen food factory, and a model center for human resource training, in conjunction of 65th Anniversary of Cambodia-Türkiye Diplomatic Relations this year
His Excellency Tan Bunpa has a meeting with Oknha Te Taing Por
On the morning of 6 December 2024, His Excellency Tan Bunpa, Ambassador of the Royal Embassy of Cambodia to Serbia, businessmen, travel agents, and journalists from the Republic of Serbia, had a courtesy call and discussed with Oknha Te Taing Por, President of the Federation of Associations for Small and Medium Enterprises of Cambodia, to learn about Cambodia’s potential in the fields of economy, small and medium enterprises and agriculture
On this occasion, Oknha Te Taing Por spoke about Cambodia’s potential in the trade sector, the export of Cambodian products to international markets and plans to export Cambodian products to the European market, as well as maintaining close relations, expanding and further strengthening relations between Cambodia and Serbia
His Excellency Tan Bunpa meets with H.E. Suon Sophal, Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodia Investment Board
