The Royal Embassy of Cambodia to the Federal Republic of Germany hosted ASEAN-Republic of Korea Working Lunch
On 19 December 2024, the Royal Embassy of Cambodia to the Federal Republic of Germany hosted the ASEAN-Republic of Korea (ROK) Working Lunch
Attendees included His Excellency Sang Beom Lim, Ambassador of the Republic of Korea, the 10 Heads of Mission of ASEAN countries, and their respective accompanying delegates, totaling 22 participants
His Excellency CHHEANG Thyra, as the Chair of the Berlin ASEAN Committee (BAC), emphasized the BAC’s efforts to strengthen friendship, solidarity, and collaboration within the ASEAN family and with ASEAN’s dialogue partners in Germany
His Excellency ambassador highlighted the progress made by ASEAN-ROK over the past 35 years, particularly noting the establishment of the ASEAN-ROK Comprehensive Strategic Partnership in early October this year
He commended the ROK's steadfast support for ASEAN community-building efforts, notably through initiatives such as the ROK-ASEAN Solidarity Initiative (KASI), among others
On the morning of January 7, 2025, His Excellency Keo Chhea, Ambassador and Permanent Representative of Cambodia to the United Nations (UN), paid a courtesy call on Her Excellency Pascale Baeriswyl, Ambassador and Permanent Representative of Switzerland to the United Nations
During the meeting, the Permanent Representative of Switzerland congratulated Cambodia on her election as a member of the Organizational Committee of the UN Peacebuilding Commission for the 2025-2026 term and looked forward to close cooperation with Cambodia to enhance the UN's peacebuilding architecture
The Permanent Representative of Cambodia shared some of Cambodia’s priority work at the UN and highlighted Cambodia’s contribution to global peacekeeping efforts through the deployment of peacekeeping forces to Africa, including in Cyprus and Lebanon
Both ambassadors also exchanged views on cooperation within ASEAN framework and the issue in Myanmar as well as committed to further strengthening good cooperation between Cambodia and Switzerland within the UN framework
Kanni Wignaraja, the UN Assistant Secretary-General and Regional Director for Asia and the Pacific at the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP)
They also exchanged views on regional and international of common concerns, notably the issues in Myanmar and transnational crimes as well as reiterated joint commitments to furthering good cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and UNDP in the coming years
