On this occasion, His Excellency the Ambassador also made a statement welcoming and appreciating the efforts in preparing the 2025 work programme of the PBC, which reflects the commitment to maintaining peace in conflict-affected areas and the importance of national ownership, inclusiveness, capacity building, and national reconciliation
Royal Embassy of Cambodia to Germany Hosts the 5th ASEAN Berlin Committee Meeting, Concludes BAC Chairmanship
On February 18, 2025, the Royal Embassy of Cambodia in Berlin, as Chair of the Berlin ASEAN Committee (BAC), hosted the 5th BAC Meeting to review the past activities and outline future directions for the BAC
The meeting also marked the official conclusion of Cambodia’s six-month chairmanship and the handover of the rotating chairmanship to Lao PDR for the next term starting in March 2025
Reflecting on Cambodia’s tenure, His Excellency CHHEANG Thyra highlighted the collective efforts made to foster ASEAN unity, strengthen friendships with Dialogue Partners, and enhance ASEAN’s visibility in Germany
He expressed deep appreciation for the unwavering support from BAC members and commended the working group's dedication throughout Cambodia’s chairmanship over the past six months, which led to the successful organization of various activities
Looking ahead, the meeting discussed future initiatives to further strengthen BAC’s role in Berlin, including hosting working lunches or dinners not only with ASEAN Dialogue Partners but also with potential private sector representatives and organizing outdoor networking events
With the transition to Laos’ leadership, His Excellency CHHEANG Thyra acknowledged the continued advancement of BAC’s work and the importance of sustaining its momentum
