Meeting with His Excellency Jonathan KINGS, New Zealand Ambassador ( 07 June 2023 )
On the morning of June 7th, 2023, Her Excellency TUOT Panha, Secretary of State on behalf of His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia, received His Excellency Jonathan KINGS, New Zealand Ambassador to the Kingdom of Cambodia with residence in Bangkok, at the Ministry
During the meeting, both sides reviewed with satisfaction the progress of the two countries’ bilateral relations
Her Excellency TUOT Panha expressed her deep appreciation towards New Zealand for her continual assistance in Cambodia’s socio-economic development
While noting the gradual increase of bilateral trade volume, both sides also discussed ways to encourage further expansion of trade and investment between the two countries
His Excellency Ambassador expressed New Zealand companies’ interests in manufacturing investment in Cambodia
Both sides agreed on the importance of closely working together in the fields of education, agriculture, renewable energy, demining, and climate resilience
The two sides also agreed on the convening of the Third Cambodia-New Zealand Foreign Ministries’ Consultations later this year to further strengthen and expand bilateral cooperation in many areas for the mutual interest of the two peoples
Additionally, the two sides had also exchanged views on regional and international matters of mutual concern and interest
