This reaffirmed the strong and long-standing ties between Cambodia and Canada, demonstrating the commitment of both governments to further enhance these relations
Secretary of State Chum Sounry took the opportunity to commend Ambassador Taylor for her efforts in strengthening the bilateral relationship during her tenure
He also expressed his appreciation to the Canadian Government for its contributions to Cambodia’s socio-economic development and for pledging additional assistance to support de-mining activities which will contribute to Cambodia’s goal of becoming a mine-free country by 2025
The two sides also discussed cooperation at multilateral fora and exchanged views on enhancing ASEAN-Canada relations
The Secretary of State reiterated Cambodia’s support for elevating the ASEAN-Canada dialogue relations to a Strategic Partnership
Both sides also noted the significance of the ongoing negotiations to establish the ASEAN-Canada Free Trade Agreement, recognizing the potential benefits it will bring to bilateral trade and economic cooperation between the region and Canada
