Désiré Nyaruhirira, Special Advisor, in charge of Politics and Diplomacy to the Secretary General of La Francophonie, for a courtesy and working meeting, during the Francophonie Electoral Mission (MEF) placed under his leadership to observe the 7th legislative elections on July 23, 2023
He emphasized that these very important 7th parliamentary elections prove Cambodia's commitment (1) to national renewal, (2) to the lasting strengthening of peace and stability, and (3) to anchoring the Kingdom of Cambodia in the rule of law and a democratic, liberal and multi-party system
Désiré Nyaruhirira expressed his gratitude to His Excellency the Secretary of State for his warm welcome and informed him of the objective of the MEF in Cambodia, stressing that Cambodia is an active and important member of the OIF
The MEF sent by the OIF to observe the elections aims to strengthen the cooperation between Cambodia and the OIF
The MEF aims to better understand the electoral process in Cambodia, through the meetings with the key actors, such as Cambodian leaders of the institutions concerned (particularly, the National Electoral Committee, the Constitutional Council and the Ministry of Interior), political parties and non-governmental organizations, as well as through observation in the field and in various polling stations
Then, the head of the delegation recalled the success of the Economic and Trade Mission of La Francophonie in Asia-Pacific (MECA) which took place in Cambodia in March 2022
