During the Official Visit to the Republic of Türkiye, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister SOK Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, gave an interview to the Anadolu Turkish News Agency, on 26 May 2024
The Deputy Prime Minister stated that the visit to Türkiye was to highlight the excellent ties between Cambodia and Türkiye on the occasion of the 65th Anniversary of the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the two countries, as well as to further deepening and expanding political, economic and cultural cooperation for the mutual benefits of the two peoples
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister SOK Chenda Sophea Encourages Türkiye Companies to Seek Investment Opportunities in Cambodia
On 27 May 2024, on the occasion of his Official Visit to the Republic of Türkiye, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister SOK Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and His Excellency Mustafa TUZCU, Deputy Minister of Trade of Türkiye, jointly addressed the Cambodia-Türkiye Business Luncheon, which was attended by over 30 company Representatives
The Deputy Prime Minister encouraged Türkiye companies to seek investment opportunities in Cambodia in potential fields, such as tourism, agriculture, agro-processing, logistics, hotel management and construction, and to choose Cambodia as a gateway to expand their investment in Southeast Asia - a vast market under the framework of the existing ASEAN Free Trade Area and Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP)
