His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister and His Excellency the Ambassador of China sign the Agreement on the Cooperation Projects of the Mekong-Lancang Cooperation (MLC) Special Fund 2024
On 5 September 2024, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and His Excellency WANG Wenbin, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the People's Republic of China, signed the Agreement on the Cooperation Projects of the Mekong-Lancang Cooperation (MLC) Special Fund 2024
This Special Fund will provide approximately USD 2 million to support eight projects in Cambodia focusing on tourism, mine action, agriculture, rural development, promotion of MLC awareness, regional economic enhancement, Technical and Vocational Education and training (TVET), capacity building, and flood risk management
This cooperation underscores our shared commitment to fostering sustainable development and enhancing cooperation among the Mekong-Lancang countries
On behalf of the Royal Government and people of Cambodia, the Deputy Prime Minister expressed gratitude to China for its continuous support to Cambodia and other MLC member countries through the MLC Special Fund, which has greatly contributed to socio-economic development in Cambodia and the Mekong sub-region
His Excellency KUNG Phoak receives a courtesy call by Mr. NAGASE Kensuke, newly appointed Minister and Deputy Chief of Mission of the Embassy of Japan to Cambodia
On the morning of 6 September 2024, His Excellency KUNG Phoak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and ASEAN SOM Leader of Cambodia, received a courtesy call by Mr
NAGASE Kensuke, newly appointed Minister and Deputy Chief of Mission of the Embassy of Japan to Cambodia, at the Ministry
His Excellency KUNG Phoak congratulated and conveyed his best wishes to Mr
NAGASE Kensuke on the occasion of his new appointment as the Minister and Deputy Chief of Mission of the Embassy of Japan to Cambodia
His Excellency Prabowo Subianto, Minister of Defence and President-elect of the Republic of Indonesia, is paying a working visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia
His Excellency Prabowo Subianto, Minister of Defence and President-elect of the Republic of Indonesia, is paying a working visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia on 6 September 2024
The visit underlines the warm relations between Cambodia and Indonesia, and maintains the good momentum of high-level exchanges and engagements by leaders of the two countries
During the visit, His Excellency Prabowo Subianto will pay courtesy calls on Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo HUN Sen, Acting Head of State, and Samdech Moha Borvor Thipadei HUN Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia
His Excellency SOM VISAL meets with His Excellency Kanat TUMYSH, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Republic of Kazakhstan to the Kingdom of Cambodia
On 05 September 2024, His Excellency SOM VISAL, Under Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, met with His Excellency Kanat TUMYSH, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Republic of Kazakhstan to the Kingdom of Cambodia with residence in Ha Noi, at the Ministry
During the meeting, His Excellency Under Secretary of State congratulated His Excellency Kanat TUMYSH on his appointment as a new Kazakh Ambassador to Cambodia and stated that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation stands ready to work closely with His Excellency Ambassador and the Embassy of Kazakhstan to promote ties of friendship and cooperation between the two countries
Both sides reviewed the development of bilateral relations and agreed to foster cooperation in the fields of trade, investment, tourism and education
They also emphasized the importance of resuming talks pertaining to the draft of MoU on Political Consultation between the two Ministries, which is a substantial mechanism for exploring new ways to foster exchanges of trade, economics, tourism and cooperation in other areas
Meanwhile, both sides also expressed commitment to further promote cooperation and support each other in bilateral and multilateral frameworks between the two nations
His Excellency Secretary of State MEAS Kim Heng has a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Igor DRIESMANS, Ambassador of the European Union to the Kingdom of Cambodia
On 06 September 2024, His Excellency MEAS Kim Heng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Igor DRIESMANS, Ambassador of the European Union to the Kingdom of Cambodia, at the Ministry
During the meeting, both sides expressed satisfaction on the progress made in Cambodia-EU relations, discussed ways to further promote bilateral trade and investments between Cambodia and the EU, and recent developments in Cambodia
Cambodia, Canada Explore Opportunities To Deepen Ties
Cambodia and Canada discussed ways to further boost relationship and cooperation in both the bilateral and ASEAN frameworks during the first Bilateral Consultations between the two Foreign Ministries co-chaired by His Excellency CHUM Sounry, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs andInternational Cooperation of Cambodia, and His Excellency Alan Bowman, Director-General for Southeast Asia and Oceania of the Global Affairs of Canada, in Ottawa, on 5 September 2024
The two sides reviewed the existing cooperation andhighlighted the actions to be followed up on some areas, which include trade and investment, demining, consular affairs and tourism, Francophonie, and werecommitted to working more closely as “trusted partner”
The ASEAN-Canada Strategic Partnership and ASEAN-Canada FTA were also touched on
During the consultations, Secretary of State Sounry was also briefed on Canada’s Indo Pacific Strategy by His Excellency Weldon Epp, Assistant Deputy Minister for Indo Pacific of the Global Affairs of Canada
Besides, Secretary of State Sounry had an exchange of views and discussion on some regional and international issues of common interests and concernswith Her Excellency Sandra McCardell, Associate Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs of Canada, in aluncheon hosted by the latter
It should be noted that the Cambodian delegation was also joined by His Excellency RATH Saravuth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, and Mr
Deputy Prime Minister receives a farewell call by outgoing Thai envoy upon his completion of tenure in Cambodia
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister SOK Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, congratulated His Excellency Cherdkiat Atthakor, Ambassador of the Kingdom of Thailand to the Kingdom of Cambodia, on the successful completion of his diplomatic mission in Cambodia, during the latter’s farewell call on 10 September 2024 at the Ministry
His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea highly valued the Ambassador’s active contribution to advancing the bilateral relations, which had been elevated to “Strategic Partnership” in February 2024
As the two countries will celebrate the 75th anniversary of diplomatic relations in 2025, both sides agreed to jointly organize events to commemorate the special year
His Excellency Ambassador extended profound appreciation to the Ministry for providing steadfast support during his mission in the Kingdom
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister and His Excellency Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia sign an Exchange of Notes for the extension of Yen loan
On 6 September 2024, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and His Excellency Ueno Atsushi, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Cambodia, signed an Exchange of Notes for the extension of Yen loan approximately JPY 7,988,000,000 (USD 55 million) to support the Phnom Penh City Transmission and Distribution System Expansion Project (Phase 2, Third Tranche)
Initiated in 2015, this ongoing project aims at enhancing the stable supply of electricity in Phnom Penh by constructing vital transmission lines and substations
By ensuring a reliable electricity supply, the project is crucial for business operations and improving livelihoods, thusfostering economic growth and attracting investment
On behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, the Deputy Prime Minister, expresses gratitude to Japan for its continued Official Development Assistance (ODA), which significantly contributes to the country’s socio-economic development across various sectors as well as for dispatching experts to support the formulation of a Clean Energy Transition Roadmap, further reinforcing the partnership in achieving sustainable energy
His Excellency KUNG Phoak has a meeting with His Excellency Nong Rong, Deputy Head of Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office of the State Council
On the morning of 9 September 2024, during the official visit to the People's Republic of China, His Excellency KUNG Phoak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and ASEAN SOM Leader of Cambodia had a meeting with His Excellency Nong Rong, Deputy Head of Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office of the State Council
During the Meeting, His Excellency the Secretary of State and His Excellency Nong Rong discussed mutually beneficial Cambodia and China relations as well as ASEAN-China relations
Both sides emphasized the importance of further deepening and broadening bilateral potential areas of concrete and practical cooperation such as digital economy, green economy, green transition and blue economy, and the development of financial, technological and logistical hubs through trade and investment, amongst other things
They also explored ways as to how to come up with tangible projects for implementation so as to further boost ASEAN-China cooperation, thus contributing to ASEAN Community building effort
His Excellency KUNG Phoak has a productive discussion with His Excellency SUN Weidong, Vice Foreign Minister and ASEAN SOM Leader of the People's Republic of China
On 08 September 2024, during the official visit to the People’s Republic of China, His Excellency KUNG Phoak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and ASEAN SOM Leader of Cambodia, had a productive discussion with His Excellency SUN Weidong, Vice Foreign Minister and ASEAN SOM Leader of the People's Republic of China, at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the People’s Republic of China
Both sides also exchanged views on regional and international issues of common interests and concerns
