Nellie GHUSAYNI, newly appointed Chief of Mission of IOM in Cambodia, at the Ministry during which the latter presented the credentials on the appointment as chief of Mission of IOM in Cambodia
Ms Nellie GHUSAYNI informed Her Excellency Secretary of State on cooperation between IOM and Cambodia’s line ministries in promoting the safeguard of Cambodian migrants and combating human trafficking in Cambodia
She also expressed high appreciation on Cambodia’s efforts in addressing migrant challenges
MOU Signing Ceremony between Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and the Ministry of Inspection
On 12 September 2024, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and His Excellency Huot Hak, Minister of Inspection signed the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Cooperation for Training on Diplomacy and International Relations between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and the Ministry of Inspection
The MoU underlines the important role of the National Institute of Diplomacy and International Relations in developing training programs for leaders and officials of the Ministry of Inspection
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea further emphasized that the cooperation aims to foster capacity-building and human resource development for government officials in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia’s Pentagonal Strategy Phase I
