Deputy Prime Minister receives a courtesy call from New Zealand’s envoy
On 18 September 2024, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister SOK Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received a courtesy call from His Excellency Jonathan Kings, Ambassador of New Zealand to the Kingdom of Cambodia with Residence in Bangkok, at the Ministry
His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea welcomed and thanked His Excellency Jonathan Kings for delivering a lecture on “65 Years of Cambodia-New Zealand Relations and New Zealand’s Policy Priorities” at National Institute of Diplomacy and International Relations
The Deputy Prime Minister recalled the productive meeting with His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister Winston Peters, Minister of Foreign Affairs of New Zealand, in July in Vientiane
The Deputy Prime Minister expressed his deep thanks to New Zealand for its assistance and suggested that the two countries work together more in the areas of agriculture, agro-processing, and human resource development
Additionally, the Deputy Prime Minister suggested that New Zealand hold business seminars in any of the ASEAN member states where a large number of New Zealanders could attend and hear from representatives of the Council for the Development of Cambodia about trade and investment opportunities in Cambodia
His Excellency Mr. SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation delivered a statement at the Summit of the Future
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister highlighted 5 key points: (1) the fragile state of international peace and security; (2) the need for financing in sustainable development; (3) the solutions and risks presented by the advancement of science, digital technologies and innovation to human development; (4) the need to engage youth in development; and (5) the importance of transforming global governance in maintaining peace, stability and achieving sustainable development goals
Deputy Prime Minister SOK Chenda Sophea had a breakfast meeting with the Foreign Ministers of Laos and Viet Nam
This is the first trilateral meeting among the three foreign ministers following the decision to hold such meetings on the sidelines of multilateral meetings, in addition to the trilateral meetings at the head of Government level, which have already been held multiple times
Bilateral Meeting between His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and His Excellency Kulubaev Zheenbek, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Kyrgyzstan
On 23 September 2024, on the occasion of attending the 79th Session of the United Nations General Assembly, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister SOK Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation had a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Zheenbek Kulubaev, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Kyrgyzstan at the United Nations Headquarters, New York
The two ministers discussed the enhancement of ties under bilateral and multilateral framework particularly in trade, investment, and people to people exchange
His Excellency Zheenbek Kulubaev expressed his intention to welcome Cambodian students in the field of medical science since Kyrgyzstan has expertise and has welcomed students from many countries in the field
On the occasion, His Excellency Deputy Prime and His Excellency Zheenbek Kulubaev signed the Memorandum of Understanding on the Establishment of Bilateral Consultations between the two foreign ministries and agreed to convene the first meeting at an early date
Kyrgyzstan is a country located in the Central Asia region with a population of approximately 7 million and forged diplomatic ties with Cambodia in 1995
Bilateral meeting between His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Her Excellency Baiba Braže, Minister for Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Latvia
On 24 September 2024, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a bilateral meeting with Her Excellency Baiba Braže, Minister for Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Latvia, during the 79th Session of the United Nations General Assembly at the United Nations headquarters in New York
Both sides exchanged views on how to further enhance bilateral relations between Cambodia and Latvia and explore opportunities for cooperation in potential sectors of mutual interest
The two foreign ministers also discussed cooperation under multilateral frameworks and regional and international issues of common interests and concerns
Her Excellency Baiba Braže expressed appreciation to the Deputy Prime Minister for the opportunity to meet and look forward to enhancing cooperation between the two countries
Bilateral meeting between His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and His Excellency Péter Szijjártó, Minister of Foreign Affairs and Trade of Hungary
On 24 September 2024, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation had a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Péter Szijjártó, Minister of Foreign Affairs and Trade of Hungary, during the 79th session of the United Nations General Assembly at the United Nations headquarters in New York
The Deputy Prime Minister expressed his high appreciation for the progress made in bilateral relations, highlighting the high level exchange of visits and the convening of bilateral talks including the Joint Economic Committee, Bilateral Consultations, and the Consultative Session on the Peace Charter between the two National Assemblies
His Excellency Péter Szijjártó expressed his sincere thanks and satisfaction for the close cooperation between the two countries
His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation attended the opening session of the General Debate of the 79th Session of the General Assembly at the United Nations
As the High Representative of Samdech Moha Borvor Thipadei HUN Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, attended the Opening Session of the General Debate of the 79th Session of the General Assembly on 24 September 2024, at the United Nations Headquarters in New York
The Meeting discussedthe indispensable role of the United Nations in addressing global challenges and underscored that only with reinvigoration ofmultilateralism will it be possible to achieve a peaceful, prosperous, sustainable, and inclusive future for all
Bilateral Meeting between His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and His Excellency Okello Oryem Henry, Minister of State for Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Uganda
On 25 September 2024, during the 79th Session of the United Nations General Assembly, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation had a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Okello Oryem Henry, Minister of State for Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Uganda, at the United Nations Headquarter, New York
The Deputy Prime Minister expressed his high appreciation to Uganda for its successful chairmanship of the Non-Aligned Movement (NAM) and for promoting the interests of member states from developing countries
Both sides discussed efforts to further promote friendly relations and bilateral cooperation
They also agreed to strengthen cooperation and extend mutual support in the regional and international fora
Bilateral Meeting between His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and H.E. Andrii Sybiha, Minister for Foreign Affairs of Ukraine
On 25 September 2024 on the sidelines of the 79th Session of the United Nations General Assembly, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation had a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Andrii Sybiha, Minister for Foreign Affairs of Ukraine, at the United Nations Headquarters, New York
Both sides discussed efforts to further promote bilateral ties and cooperation in multilateral framework
After their productive meeting, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister and His Excellency Andrii Sybiha, signed the Agreement on Visa Exemption for Holders of Diplomatic,Service or Official Passports
Bilateral meeting between His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooepration and His Excellency Kurt Campbell, United States Deputy Secretary of State
On 25 September 2024, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, held a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Kurt Campbell, US Deputy Secretary of State, in New York
Both sides expressed satisfaction with the progress in bilateral relations and pledged to enhance engagement to further strengthen their ties
They also discussed multilateral cooperation, particularly within the ASEAN framework, where Cambodia took on the role of country coordinator for ASEAN-US Dialogue Relations ( 2024 - 2027)
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister meets the newly appointed Minister for Europe and Foreign Affairs of France
On 25 September 2024, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, met with His Excellency Jean-Noël Barrot, the newly appointed Minister for Europe and Foreign Affairs of France, on the sidelines of the 79th session of the United Nations General Assembly in New York
The French Foreign Minister looks forward to meeting the Deputy Prime Minister at the 19th Francophonie Summit in Paris from 3 to 5 October 2024
His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation attended the Group of Twenty (G20) Foreign Ministers’ Meeting
This marks the first time that the G20 has invited all UN Member States to attend this meeting, underscoring the importance of inclusiveness and multilateralism
Meeting between His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Her Excellency Julie Bishop, Special Envoy of the United Nations Secretary-General on Myanmar
On 25 September 2024, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation had a meeting with Her Excellency Julie Bishop, Special Envoy of the United Nations Secretary-General on Myanmar
The Deputy Prime Minister expressed warm welcome on the appointment of Her Excellency Julie Bishop as the Special Envoy of the UN Secretary-General on Myanmar
He also shared Cambodia’s position on Myanmar including supporting engagement with Myanmar and ASEAN’s mechanisms namely ASEAN special envoy, Troika, and expanded Troika
His Excellency Secretary of State KAN Pharidh meets with His Excellency Dominic Williams, Ambassador of the United Kingdom to Cambodia
On 26 September 2024, His Excellency KAN Pharidh, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, met with His Excellency Dominic Williams, Ambassador of the United Kingdom to Cambodia, at the Ministry
His Excellency Secretary of State welcomed the visit of the British naval ship, HMS SPEY (P234), docked at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, recognizing its contribution to enhancing bilateral relations between the two countries
The discussions also covered regional and international matters, as well as cooperation within the UN framework
Meeting between His Excellency SOK Chenda Sopea,Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and Mr. Michael Goltzman,Senior Vice-President, Global Policy and Sustainability of the Coca-Cola Company
Michael Goltzman, Senior Vice-President, Global Policy and Sustainability of the Coca-Cola Company at the Permanent Mission of Cambodia in New York
The Deputy Prime Minister thanked Coca Cola for trust in the Royal Government of Cambodia through investment in a huge factory and for corporate social responsibility activities
Deputy Prime Minister attended the roundtable dinner hosted by the Business Council for International Understanding
On the occasion of attending the 79th Session of the United Nations General Assembly on 26 September 2024, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, attended the roundtable dinner hosted by the Business Council for International Understanding (BCIU) with participations from several US companies
The Deputy Prime Minister briefed on the progress of socio-economic development and policy to promote investments in Cambodia as well as answered to questions from participants on the economy and investment climate in Cambodia
He also expressed his pledge to promote US investments in Cambodia
Bilateral meeting between His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and His Excellency Rashid Meredov, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Turkmenistan
On 28 September 2024 on the sidelines of the 79th Session of the United Nations General Assembly, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Rashid Meredov, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Turkmenistan, at the United Nations Headquarters, New York
Both sides discussed efforts to further promote friendship and cooperation, particularly in exchanges of visits of leaders, businessmen, trade, investment and tourism of the two countries
After the meeting, the Deputy Prime Minister and His Excellency Rashid Meredov, signed a Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Turkmenistan on the Establishment of Bilateral Consultations
Bilateral meeting between His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and His Excellency Yván Gil Pinto, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela
On 28 September 2024 on the sidelines of the 79th Session of the United Nations General Assembly, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Yván Gil Pinto, Minister of the People's Power for Foreign Affairs of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela at the United Nations Headquarter, New York
The Deputy Prime Minister is pleased that despite geographical distance, Cambodia always attaches great importance to deepening and enhancing friendly ties and cooperation with Venezuela, as well as other countries in Latin America
His Excellency Yván Gil Pinto expressed sincere thanks to the Deputy Prime Minister for the opportunity to meet during the busy time of UNGA79 and conveyed appreciation for the close cooperation between the two countries
Both sides exchanged views on regional and international issues of common concern
Deputy Prime Minister SOK Chenda Sophea attended the High-Level Reception hosted by President Joe Biden
On 25 September 2024, as the High Representative of Samdech Moha Borvor Thipadei HUN Manet, Prime minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, attended a High-Level Reception at the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York, at the invitation of His Excellency Joe Biden, President of the United States of America
His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, delivered a national statement at the General Debate of the 79th Session of the United Nations
