Meeting between His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and His Excellency António Guterres, Secretary-General of the United Nations
On 28 September 2024, on the occasion of attending the 79th Session of the United Nations General Assembly, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a meeting with His Excellency António Guterres, UN Secretary-General at the United Nations Headquarters, in New York
The Deputy Prime Minister informed that Cambodia waspleased to warmly welcome four official visits of Under-Secretary-General of the United Nations between May and July this year
This reflects the close relations and cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the United Nations
Furthermore, the Deputy Prime Minister also informed that despite being a small country that has endureddecades of war, Cambodia now proudly contributes troops to UN Peacekeeping Operations
The Secretary-General thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Deputy Prime Minister for Cambodia’ssignificant contributions of UN Peacekeeping Operationsworldwide
He also expressed his satisfaction for the close cooperation between Cambodia and the UN in various fields and praised Cambodia for its remarkable socio-economic development
The two sides also exchanged views on key regional andglobal issues of common concern and reaffirmed their commitment to continue cooperation
His Excellency KHUON Phon Rattanak holds a virtual meeting with President of the Foundation Board of the Liechtenstein Development Service (LED)
Peter BECK, President of the Foundation Board of the Liechtenstein Development Service (LED)
