His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea holds a productive telephone conversation with His Excellency IWAYA Takeshi, the newly appointed Minister for Foreign Affairs of Japan
On 21 October 2024, His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, held a productive telephone conversation with His Excellency IWAYA Takeshi, the newly appointed Minister for Foreign Affairs of Japan
During the call, His Excellency the Deputy Prime Ministerrenewed his congratulations on His Excellency IWAYA Takeshi’s appointment
The two Ministers engaged in a wide-ranging discussion on bilateral relations and expressed satisfaction with the progress of the enduring friendly relationship and multifaceted cooperation
Both sides reaffirmed their shared resolve to further strengthen the Comprehensive Strategic Partnership between the two countries
The Deputy Prime Minister recalled Japan’s significant contribution to Cambodia’s peace and reconstruction processand expressed gratitude to Japan for continuous assistance in supporting Cambodia’s socio-economic development
His Excellency IWAYA Takeshi expressed his commitment to further promote the existing excellent cooperation including in trade and investment, education, health, defense and security, demining, and connectivity
The two ministers also exchanged views on regional and international issues of common concern
A phone conversation between Cambodian Foreign Minister and the newly appointed Indonesian Foreign Minister
His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, and His Excellency Sugiono, the newly appointed Minister of Foreign Affairs of Indonesia, spoke highly of the long-standing relations between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Indonesia, during a phone conversation on 23 October 2024
The two Foreign Ministers recalled the long-lasting friendly relations between the two countries, which were established by the Late King Father, His Majesty Preah Bat Samdech Preah NORODOM SIHANOUK, Preah BOROM RATANAK KAUDH, and the Late President Sukarno in 1959 and their special affinity
The two Foreign Ministers expressed their satisfaction over the growing ties of friendship and cooperation and reaffirmedtheir strong commitment to work closely together to further promote warm relations and deepen cooperation in multiple areas, including politics, defense and security, trade and investment, education and culture
The Deputy Prime Minister renewed his warmest congratulations to His Excellency Sugiono on his appointment as Foreign Minister of Indonesia and looked forward to meeting him in person
His Excellency KAN Pharidh receives a courtesy call by His Excellency SOK Piseth, Secretary-General and Vice Chairman of the Board of the Youth House for Cambodia-China Friendship
On behalf of His Excellency SOK Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, on 23 October 2024, His Excellency KAN Pharidh, Secretary of State, received a courtesy call by His Excellency SOK Piseth, Secretary-General and Vice Chairman of the Board of the Youth House for Cambodia-China Friendship, which is the local Non-Governmental Organization, at the Ministry
During discussion, His Excellency SOK Piseth outlined the action plans focusing on education and leadership between two countries, through providing scholarships to Cambodian students to study in China, and organizing young leadership forums to exchange views and best practices in promoting youth-to-youth connectivity as well as people-to-people connectivity
In response, His Excellency Secretary of State raised the priority fields and activities aimed at navigating the implementation of the organization’s activities
