Cambodia-Kazakhstan to strengthen bilateral ties
On 31 October 2024, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister SOK Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received a courtesy call by His Excellency Kanat TUMYSH, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Republic of Kazakhstan to the Kingdom of Cambodia with residence in Hanoi, Vietnam, at the Ministry
The Deputy Prime Minister and the Ambassador celebrated the launch of direct flights between Cambodia and Kazakhstan, a significant step towards enhancing people-to-people connectivity, tourism, and business opportunities for both nations
Both sides underscored a shared commitment to advancing the Bilateral Consultation Framework—a strategic platform designed to foster continuous, open dialogue, and strengthen both diplomatic and economic ties
They expressed a mutual ambition to explore new potentials for trade, particularly in the agricultural sector
Meanwhile, both sides also expressed their commitment to continuing to strengthen and deepen cooperation as well as support each other in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks, particularly in framework of CICA
Meeting Between His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister and Ambassador of Australia
On 01 November 2024, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister SOK Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received a courtesy call by His Excellency Derek YIP, Ambassador of Australia to the Kingdom of Cambodia, at the Ministry
His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister reflected on the strong and enduring ties between the two countries, and they reaffirmed the robust partnership and shared commitment to mutual growth and cooperation that has marked the bilateral relationship since the establishment of diplomatic relations
His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister expressed profound appreciation for Australia’s long-standing support for Cambodia, highlighting its pivotal role in areas, such as capacity building, social development, and digital transformation
He also shared insights on the Royal Government of Cambodia’s Pentagonal Strategy, an overarching framework aimed at advancing national development
Both sides shared the commitment to further deepening cooperation across a range of sectors to foster a resilient partnership for the mutual benefits of both nations
