His Excellency KHUON Phon Ratthanak and His Excellency Charles Hay co-chair the Second Round of Bilateral Consultations
On 7-8 November 2024, His Excellency KHUON Phon Rattanak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and His Excellency Charles Hay, Director for Indo-Pacific of the Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office, co-chaired the Second Round of Bilateral Consultations between the two Foreign Ministries in London, the United Kingdom
Both sides expressed satisfaction with the flourishing relations between Cambodia and the UK, highlighting significant advancements in the areas of politics, economics, trade, investment and development
Both dignitaries reaffirmed commitments to deepen political and economic cooperation between Cambodia and the UK
A number of regional and global issues of mutual interest were also touched upon
His Excellency Secretary also met with Professor Colin Bailey, President and Principal of Queen Mary University of London, to explore potential avenues for educational cooperation, and he met with Cambodian students studying at the university
This round of successful Bilateral Consultations represents a steady and essential step forward in advancing cooperation for the reciprocal benefits of both countries
