Felipe DE MORENA CASADO, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Kingdom of Spain to the Kingdom of Cambodia with resident in Bangkok, Thailand
Both sides noted with deep satisfaction the traditional relations and good cooperation between the two Kingdoms and discussed ways to elevate further bilateral cooperation in trade, investment, and other spheres of mutual interest
He took the opportunity to convey Cambodia’s deepest condolences to the Spanish government and people for the recent devastating flooding in the Valencia region
His Excellency the Ambassador congratulated Cambodia on hosting the upcoming Siem Reap-Angkor Summit on a Mine-Free World and commended Cambodia’s contributions to UN peacekeeping missions
He reaffirmed his unwavering commitment to promoting two-way trade and investment between the two countries
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhonn Shares Cambodia’s Peace Experiences
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, shared Cambodia’s experiences in contributing to global peace by dispatching the Cambodian blue helmets to take part in the United Nations peacekeeping operations worldwide, which were highly appreciated by the international community
The sharing was presented on 24 November 2024 in the 1st Plenary Session on “Advancing the Global Architecture of Peace, Peace Building, Reconciliation, and Tolerance: Synergy of Governments, Parliaments, and Civil Society” of the 11th Plenary Session of the International Parliament for Tolerance and Peace (IPTP 11), which is being held in Cambodia from 23 to 26 November 2024
In his presentation, the Deputy Prime Minister emphasized that peace and stability have been pivotal in Cambodia’s economic and social development, as well as the integration of the country into regional and international organizations
Furthermore, the prevalence of peace in the country has fostered Cambodia’s contribution to global peace process
Her Excellency Secretary of State EAT Sophea receives a courtesy call by Parliamentary Vice Minister for Foreign Affairs of Japan
On behalf of His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Her Excellency EAT Sophea, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Advisor to Samdech Moha Borvor Thipadei HUN Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, received a courtesy call by Her Excellency ERI Arfiya, Parliamentary Vice Minister for Foreign Affairs of Japan, on the afternoon of 26 November 2024, at the Ministry
Her Excellency EAT Sophea expressed her welcome and appreciation to Her Excellency ERI Arfiya for the participation in the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit on a Mine-Free World in Siem Reap province
In response, Her Excellency ERI Arfiya expressed her thankfulness for warm welcome and cordial hospitality extended to her and the Japanese delegation, especially an opportunity to pay a courtesy call on Samdech Thipadei Prime Minister
Her Excellency EAT Sophea and Her Excellency ERI Arfiya discussed the strengthening and deepening of Cambodia-Japan Comprehensive Strategic Partnership, and the importance of new cooperation approach focusing on three key areas, such as social infrastructure development, maritime connectivity and mine action
On behalf of His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, His Excellency KHUON Phon Rattanak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, met with His Excellency Andreas Motzfeldt Kravik, Vice Minister of Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Kingdom of Norway on 26 November 2024, at the Ministry
His Excellency KHUON Phon Rattanak expressed his warm welcome and appreciation to His Excellency Andreas Motzfeldt Kravik for his participation in the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit on a Mine-Free World
He also expressed his sincere gratitude to Norwegian government for being a long-time supporter of demining activities in Cambodia since early 1990s as well as for its contribution to the Extraordinary Chamber in the Court of Cambodia
In response, His Excellency Andreas Motzfeldt Kravik expressed his thanks for warm welcome and cordial hospitality extended to him and the Norwegian delegation, especially an opportunity to pay a courtesy call on Samdech Thipadei Prime Minister
Both sides also discussed further deepening and strengthening bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and Norway especially in economic development and investment
They also exchanged views on multilateral cooperation such as ASEAN and international law
His Excellency KUNG Phoak attends the ASEAN-Republic of Korea Day in Commemoration of the 35th Anniversary of Dialogue Relations and the Establishment of the Comprehensive Strategic Partnership (CSP)
His Excellency Secretary of State Meas Kim Heng receives His Excellency Viorel Stefan, Member of the European Court of Auditors
On 26 November 2024, His Excellency Meas Kim Heng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received His Excellency Viorel Stefan, Member of the European Court of Auditors, at the Ministry
During the meeting, both sides exchanged views on Cambodia’s development priorities, the effectiveness of EU development assistance, and Cambodia’s LDC graduation
His Excellency Stefan informed that his mission is to conduct audit on EU’s Aid for Trade assistance in Cambodia and assess the effectiveness of EU support for Cambodia
He also had bilateral meetings with relevant Ministries in Phnom Penh and conducted field visits to the EU’s sponsored projects
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, His Excellency Secretary of State Meas Kim Heng expressed Cambodia’s deep appreciation for the EU assistance in Cambodia and for incorporating important priorities under the Pentagonal Strategy Phase I into the Joint European Strategy for Development Cooperation with Cambodia 2021-2027 and pointed out the necessity to extend the LDC graduation from 2027 to 2029
Both sides shared the same views about the effectiveness of EU assistance in Cambodia
