Her Excellency EAT Sophea attends the reception to celebrate Russia’s Day
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Her Excellency EAT Sophea, Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, as the guest of honour, delivered a toast remarks at the reception to celebrate Russia’s Day on the evening of 11 June 2025 at Sofitel Phnom Penh
Her Excellency Acting Minister highlighted the rich culture and captivating histories of Cambodia and Russia, which are the common values of the two countries in advancing social development, including through the promotion of cultural expression, science, technology and diplomacy
Her Excellency Acting Minister also highlighted the growing cooperation between Cambodia and Russia in bilateral and multilateral frameworks across a wide range of sectors, including trade, investment, scientific collaboration, cultural exchange, defense cooperation, and tourism
Russia’s Day is celebrated annually on 12 June, to mark the establishment of the Russian Federation
The reception was hosted by His Excellency Anatoly Borovik, Ambassador of the Russian Federation to Cambodia, and attended by Cambodian dignitaries and foreign diplomats in Cambodia
The Signing of MoU on the Establishment of Political Consultations between the Foreign Ministries of Cambodia and Chile
On 12 June 2025, Her Excellency EAT Sophea, Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and His Excellency Patricio Powell Osorio, Ambassador of the Republic of Chile to the Kingdom of Cambodia, with Residence in Bangkok, signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on the Establishment of Political Consultations between the Foreign Ministries of Cambodia and Chile
Her Excellency EAT Sophea exchanged views with Ambassador Patricio Powell Osorio on strengthening and deepening bilateral relations and cooperation in potential areas, such as trade, investment, tourism, and people-to-people connectivity
Both sides also expressed commitment to further enhancing cooperation in international fora and emphasized the importance of bilateral consultations between the two Foreign Ministries
