Deputy Prime Minister leads the Heads of Foreign Diplomatic Missions to Cambodia to inspect the areas affected by the recent armed clashes between Cambodia and Thailand over border disputes
On the morning of 01 August 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, led the Heads of Foreign Diplomatic Missions accredited to the Kingdom of Cambodia on a field visit to inspect the areas affected by the recent armed clashes between Cambodia and Thailand over border disputes in Oddar Meanchey Province
During the visit, His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister also took the opportunity to visit displaced persons in the province
In the meantime, His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister paid a visit to the frontline Cambodian troops stationed at the conflict zone, offering words of encouragement and distributing humanitarian supplies in recognition of their courage and commitment
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister attends the 7th-day memorial ceremony of the late Second Lieutenant RIN Veasna, who made the ultimate sacrifice in defense of Cambodia’s territorial integrity and sovereignty
On the afternoon of 31 July 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, led the Ministry’s delegation to attend the 7th-day memorial ceremony of the late Second Lieutenant RIN Veasna, who made the ultimate sacrifice in defense of Cambodia’s territorial integrity and sovereignty at the Mom Bei battlefield in Oddar Meanchey Province on 27 July 2025
Deputy Prime Minister leads a delegation of 22 Heads of Foreign Diplomatic Missions to Cambodia and 4 representatives of UN Agencies to visit the displaced civilians
On the morning of 2 August 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, led a delegation of 22 Heads of Foreign Diplomatic Missions accredited to the Kingdom of Cambodia, along with 4 representatives of the United Nations Agencies, to visit the displaced civilians staying in the makeshift shelters, located in Sautr Nikom, Siem Reap Province
Her Excellency EAT Sophea has a cordial conversation with 25 Cambodian students
On 31 July 2025, Her Excellency EAT Sophea, Permanent Secretary of State of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a cordial conversation with 25 Cambodian students who are set to commence their studies in August 2025 under the scholarship of Human Resource Development (JDS) and the Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology of Japan (MEXT) for Master and Doctoral Degrees
The 25 students will pursue their studies at various universities in Japan in the fields of International Relations, Public Administration, Economics, Infrastructure, Agriculture and Rural Development, Education and Healthcare
His Excellency KAN Pharidh and His Excellency UN Kheang lead a delegation to visit four displaced persons camps
His Excellency KAN Pharidh and His Excellency UN Kheang, Secretaries of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation (MFAIC), led a delegation comprising representatives from 11 diplomatic missions and 15 UN agencies based in Cambodia to visit four displaced persons camps in Oddar Meanchey and Siem Reap Provinces on 6-7 August 2025
On that occasion, the delegation witnessed the hardships faced by the displaced persons and heard their greatest wishes: food, shelters, ceasefire and the ability to return home
The delegation from MFAIC also brought donations of rice and medicines to the Chong Kal displaced persons camp in Oddar Meanchey Province and the Srei Snam displaced persons camp in Siem Reap Province
Virtual Meeting between His Excellency Secretary of State KHUON Phon Rattanak and His Excellency Dr. Tibor BALOGHDI
On the morning of 6 August 2025, His Excellency KHUON Phon Rattanak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of, held a video meeting with His Excellency Dr
ASEAN Flag Hoisting Ceremony to commemorate the 58th anniversary of ASEAN’s establishment
On the morning of 8 August 2025, Her Excellency EAT Sophea, Permanent Secretary of State, on behalf of His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, presided over the ASEAN Flag Hoisting Ceremony at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, with the participation of distinguished heads and representatives of ASEAN member states and other foreign diplomatic missions to Cambodia
The event was held to commemorate the 58th anniversary of ASEAN’s establishment in 1967 and highlighted the ASEAN’s enduring spirit of regional solidarity and cooperation, as well as the shared commitment to peace, stability, and sustainable development
His Excellency PRAK Phalla participates in a high-level consultative meeting on the Draft Budget Revenue and Expenditure Expenditure Plan for 2026
On the morning of 11 August 2025, His Excellency PRAK Phalla, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, led a delegation to participate in a high-level consultative meeting on the Draft Budget Revenue and Expenditure Plan for 2026, held at the Ministry of Economy and Finance
As a result, the 2026 Draft Budget Plan received support from the Ministry of Economy and Finance, serving as a driving force for further strengthening and expanding cooperation both regionally and globally
The Ministry's delegation pays tribute to the late H.E. Mr. U Myint Swe, Pro Tempore President of Myanmar
On the afternoon of 11 August 2025, Her Excellency Eat Sophea, Permanent Secretary of State, led a delegation to pay tribute and write messages on the Book of Condolences at the Embassy of Myanmar in Phnom Penh on the passing of H
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister participates in the celebration of the 60th Anniversary of Singapore’s National Day
On the evening of 11 August 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation participated in the celebration of the 60th Anniversary of Singapore’s National Day at Raffles Le Royal Hotel, Phnom Penh
His Excellency Meas Kim Heng leads a delegation of 43 Cambodian Foreign Non-Governmental Organizations (FNGOs) on a field visit to the camps of displaced people
On 11 August 2025, His Excellency Meas Kim Heng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, led a delegation of 43 Cambodian Foreign Non-Governmental Organizations (FNGOs), comprising a total of 73 participants, on a field visit to the camps of displaced people in Banteay Ampil District, Oddar Meanchey Province, and Srey Snam District, Siem Reap Province
During the visit, the FNGOs representatives were impressed by the people’s desire for peace and stability, as well as their concerns about unexploded ordnance in their villages and the effects of the war
From their conversations with the displaced people, many of the FNGOs representatives felt that Cambodia was not the party that initiated the conflict with Thailand
His Excellency the Secretary of State also handed over donations to the displaced people, comprising a total of 11 tons of rice—of which 3 tons were contributed by the Cambodian Embassy in Japan and Cambodian citizens residing there—along with food items, such as canned fish, dried fish, sausages, bottled water, instant Khmer noodles, fish sauce, soy sauce, mosquito nets, blankets, scarves, and various medicines, most of which were provided by the FNGOs
On the morning of 12 August 2025, His Excellency UN Kheang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, met with His Excellency Bawitlung Vanlalvawna, Ambassador of the Republic of India to Cambodia, at the Ministry
During the meeting, both sides highly valued the long-standing friendship and close cooperation between Cambodia and India, as evidenced by the frequent exchanges of visits between leaders of the two countries
They also discussed ways to further expand mutually beneficial cooperation and exchanged views on preparations for upcoming high-level visits, including the planned official visit of the Cambodian leadership to India and the reciprocal visit of the Indian leadership to Cambodia
Commencement ceremony for the Training Course on “Diplomatic Tradecraft and Protocol”
Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn leads a delegation to attend the 10th Mekong-Lancang Foreign Ministers’ Meeting
On 13 August 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, led a delegation to attend the 10th Mekong-Lancang Foreign Ministers’ Meeting, to be held on 14-15 August 2025 in Anning, Yunnan Province, China
His Excellency KHUON Phon Rattanak has a cordial meeting with 24 Cambodian students
On 13 August 2025, His Excellency KHUON Phon Rattanak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a cordial meeting with 24 Cambodian students who have been awarded scholarships to pursue their studies abroad for the academic year 2025-2026 in France, Ireland, Canada, Japan, China and the Republic of Korea
The students will pursue their Master’s and Doctoral Degrees in the fields of Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Civil Engineering, International Security and Conflict Studies, Public Policy and Development Practice
His Excellency the Secretary of State warmly congratulated those students on their outstanding achievements and advised them to excel in their studies while embracing the cultures of their respective host countries
He wished all the students a safe journey and great success in their academic endeavors
Cambodian, Chinese Foreign Ministers Hold Bilateral Meeting
On the morning of 14 August 2025, His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, held a bilateral Meeting with His Excellency WANG Yi, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People’s Republic of China, on the margins of the 10th Mekong-Lancang Cooperation Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Anning City, Yunnan Province, China
On this occasion, the two foreign ministers committed to strengthening their collaboration with all countries in the Mekong region and building a peaceful, prosperous, and sustainable future, working together through the Mekong-Lancang Cooperation framework
Both sides also explored ways to further deepen friendship relations between the two countries
His Excellency Dr. UN Kheang briefs diplomatic corps from Pakistan, Australia and India on border situation
His Excellency SUN Sovanna has a cordial meeting with six outstanding Cambodian students
On 13 August 2025, His Excellency SUN Sovanna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a cordial meeting with six outstanding Cambodian students who have been awarded scholarships to pursue their Master’s degrees in Mathematics and Computer Science Engineering at ENSIIE and École Polytechnique in France for the 2025–2026 academic year
His Excellency the Secretary of State warmly congratulated the students on their achievements and encouraged them to excel in their studies and embrace new experiences
He also advised them to foster friendships and actively contribute to promoting the culture and prestige of Cambodia
He wished all the students a safe journey and great success in their academic endeavors
Informal Consultation between Cambodian, Chinese and Thai Foreign Ministers
On 14 August 2025, His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had an Informal Consultation with His Excellency WANG Yi, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People’s Republic of China and His Excellency Maris Sangiampongsa, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Thailand, on the sidelines of the 10th Mekong-Lancang Cooperation Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Anning City, Yunnan Province, China
10th Mekong-Lancang Cooperation Foreign Ministers’ Meeting
On the morning of 15 August 2025, His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, led Cambodian delegations to participate in the 10th Mekong-Lancang Cooperation Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in a rich history and scenic city of Anning, Yunnan Province, China
This high-level political and diplomatic dialogue serves as an important platform for all countries in the Mekong region to promote economic integration, connectivity and sustainable development
Bilateral Discussion between Foreign Ministers of Cambodia and Viet Nam
On the morning of the same day, His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a bilateral discussions with His Excellency BUI Thanh Son, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Socialist Republic of Viet Nam, in conjunction with the 10th Mekong-Lancang Cooperation Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Anning City, Yunnan Province, China
Bilateral Talks between Foreign Ministers of Cambodia and Myanmar
On evening of 14 August 2025, His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a bilateral talks with His Excellency U Than Swe, Deputy Prime Minister, Union Minister for Foreign Affairs of the Republic of the Union of Myanmar, on the margins of the 10th Mekong-Lancang Cooperation Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Anning City, Yunnan Province, China
Her Excellency Eat Sophea meets with Regional Director for the Asia-Pacific of the International Committee of the Red Cross
On the morning of 15 August,2025, Her Excellency Eat Sophea, Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, met with His Excellency Régis Savioz, Regional Director for the Asia-Pacific of the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) at the Head Office of the Foreign Ministry
The two sides discussed efforts of the ICRC in protecting the rights of prisoners of war and displaced people in armed conflicts, promoting respect for the international humanitarian law, and the humanitarian activities of the ICRC in Cambodia
Her Excellency Eat Sophea expressed deep appreciation for the ICRC’s humanitarian activities in Cambodia since 1979
His Excellency KAN Pharidh holds a discussion with Mr. Sardar Umar Alam and Mr. Bryan Fornari
