Her Excellency Eat Sophea briefs members of Diplomatic Corps and UN agencies in Cambodia on the latest developments in the Cambodia-Thailand border situation
Her Excellency Eat Sophea totally rejected the allegation that Cambodia had laid new landmines and reaffirmed Cambodia's commitment to achieving peace and peaceful resolution to the Cambodian-Thailand border dispute
Her Excellency Eat Sophea also touched on the outcome of the Tea Chat Meeting participated by the Foreign Ministers of Cambodia-China-Thailand on the sidelines of the Mekong-Lancang Foreign Ministers' Meeting, held on 14 August 2025 in Anning, Yunnan, China
His Excellency Meas Kim Heng presides over the 4th Consultation Meeting between the Royal Government of Cambodia and Foreign Non-Governmental Organizations (FNGOs)
On 15 August 2025, His Excellency Meas Kim Heng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation presided over the 4th Consultation Meeting between the Royal Government of Cambodia and Foreign Non-Governmental Organizations (FNGOs) under the theme “Strengthening Effective and Productive Partnership with FNGOs for Sustainable Development in Cambodia”
The Meeting was attended by 21 representatives from Cambodia’s line-ministries and 282 representatives of FNGOs (276 FNGOs)
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister brings Preah Vossa candles and other offerings to monks
On the morning of 17 August 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, accompanied by the Ministry's leaders and officials, brought Preah Vossa candles (Buddhist Lent candles) and many other offerings to the monks staying at Sbov Rik Pagoda, located in Sbov Rik Village, Leach Commune; and Keo Uddom Pagoda (called Kandal Pagoda) in Kol Totueng Village, Santreae Commune, Phnom Kravanh District, Pursat Province
