Sam Ath Sambath Sreysour, Under-Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received a courtesy call by His Excellency Faiyaz Murshid Kazi, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the People’s Republic of Bangladesh to the Kingdom of Cambodia, with residence in Bangkok, at the Ministry
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister receives a courtesy call by newly appointed UNDP Resident Representative to Cambodia
On the morning of 20 August 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received a courtesy call from Mr
Enrico Gaveglia, the newly appointed United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) Resident Representative to the Kingdom of Cambodia, who presented his Letter of Credence
Enrico Gaveglia highly commended the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia in promoting development across all sectors and reaffirmed UNDP’s commitment to strengthening cooperation with Cambodian line ministries to achieve sustainable development goals
Cambodian Foreign Minister briefs Diplomatic Corps and United Nations Agencies on the latest developments of Cambodian-Thai border conflict
On the afternoon of 21 August 2025, at the Ministry, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and international Cooperation, chaired a briefing on the latest developments of Cambodian-Thai border conflict for 42 members of the diplomatic corps and 22 United Nations Agencies accredited to the Kingdom of Cambodia
His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister underlined Cambodia’s firm commitment to upholding the ceasefire between Cambodia and Thailand, reached on 28 July 2025 in Putrajaya
He also briefed the meeting on the outcomes of Extraordinary Meeting of the General Border Committee (GBC) between Cambodia and Thailand, held on 7 August 2025 in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia
At the same time, His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister apprised the meeting of the landmine situation in Cambodia, especially along Cambodian-Thai border, while reiterating Cambodia’s strong adherence to the Convention on the Prohibition of Anti-Personnel Mines (Ottawa Convention)
He also roughly touched on the upcoming field visit to Banteay Meanchey and Oddar Meanchey provinces, scheduled on 22–23 August 2025
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister attends the celebration of the 80th Anniversary of Vietnam’s National Day
On the evening of 21 August 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, attended the celebration of the 80th Anniversary of Vietnam’s National Day
Her Excellency Mrs. EAT Sophea receives a courtesy call from Mrs. Kyung-nan Park
EAT Sophea, Permanent Secretary of State for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received a courtesy call from Mrs
Kyung-nan Park, the new Representative and Country Director of the World Food Programme (WFP) to Cambodia, who presented her credentials
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister leads a delegation to conduct site visits to the areas affected by the armed clashes between Cambodia and Thailand
This marks the fourth visit organised by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation for the delegation, with the aim of providing them with an opportunity to witness the actual situation along the Cambodian-Thai border
The Fifth Senior Officials’ Talks (5th SOTs) in Canberra, Australia
Un Kheang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and Her Excellency Michelle Chan, Deputy Secretary of the Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade of Australia, co-chaired the Fifth Senior Officials’ Talks (5th SOTs) in Canberra, Australia
The two sides expressed satisfaction with the long-standing relations between the two countries and explored ways to further elevate bilateral ties
They also exchanged views on regional and international issues of shared interest and concern
The Third Foreign Ministries’ Consultations between Cambodia and New Zealand
Un Kheang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and Her Excellency Joanna Kempkers, Divisional Manager of South and South East Asia of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade of New Zealand, co-chaired the Third Foreign Ministries’ Consultations (3rd FMCs) between Cambodia and New Zealand in Wellington, New Zealand
They also exchanged views on regional and international issues of common concern and interest
At the conclusion of the consultations, both sides agreed to convene the 4th FMCs in 2026 in Siem Reap, Cambodia
On 21 August 2025, on the sidelines of the 10th FEALAC Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Ulaanbaatar, His Excellency CHUM Sounry, Secretary of State and Head of Delegation of Cambodia, held bilateral discussions with his Colombian counterpart, Ambassador Manuel Solano, Executive Secretary of the Colombia National Committee for Pacific Economic Cooperation (COLPECC), Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Colombia
His Excellency Sounry highlighted the importance of deepening cooperation in trade, education and capacity building, demining, and tourism
Both sides emphasized the intention to hold the 3rd Bilateral Consultation between their Foreign Ministries early next year
On education, he expressed appreciation for Colombia’s offer to provide Spanish language training to Cambodian diplomats by sending Colombian instructors to Cambodia, with the academic institutes of the two Foreign Ministries continuing coordination
Cambodian Foreign Minister receives a courtesy call by Ambassador of Timor-Leste to Cambodia
On the morning of 25 August 2025, at the Ministry, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received a courtesy call by His Excellency Marcos dos Reis da Costa, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Democratic Republic of Timor-Leste to the Kingdom of Cambodia
During the meeting, His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister assured His Excellency the Ambassador of all necessary support and assistance to facilitate his diplomatic mission in further promoting friendly relations and close cooperation between Cambodia and Timor-Leste
His Excellency the Ambassador also extended his gratitude for Cambodia’s strong support for Timor-Leste’s full ASEAN membership
Her Excellency EAT Sophea receives a joint courtesy call from Ambassador of Italy and of the Holy
On the morning of 21 August 2025, Her Excellency EAT Sophea, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received a joint courtesy call from His Excellency Paolo Dionisi, Ambassador of Italy, and His Excellency Peter B
During the meeting, Her Excellency the Permanent Secretary of State commended the Ambassadors for their efforts in promoting and strengthening the ties, friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and Italy and between Cambodia and the Holy See
His Excellency CHUM Sounry attends the 10th Foreign Ministers’ Meeting of the Forum for East Asia-Latin America Cooperation
As the high representative of His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, His Excellency CHUM Sounry, Secretary of State led a delegation to attend the 10th Foreign Ministers’ Meeting of the Forum for East Asia-Latin America Cooperation (FEALAC FMM) held in Ulaanbaatar, Mongolia from 20—22 August, 2025
Before the Ministerial Session, at the 24th Senior Officials’ Meeting on 21 August, His Excellency CHUM Sounry delivered his intervention on the New FEALAC Action Plan, reaffirming Cambodia’s strong support for the Forum’s future direction
He stressed that “the Plan must remain inclusive, practical, and responsive to the priorities of all members, particularly developing countries
” At the 10th Foreign Ministers’ Meeting on 22 August, His Excellency CHUM Sounry, in his capacity as representative of H
He stressed that “the future strength of FEALAC depends on vision, structure, commitment, and concrete action
” On the sidelines of the FMM, His Excellency Sounry paid a courtesy call on Her Excellency Battsetseg Batmunkh, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Mongolia, and Co-chair of the 10th FEALAC FMM, and held talks with Heads of Delegation of Colombia and Chile
It is noted that FEALAC comprises 36 member states: 16 from East Asia, including all ASEAN countries, and 20 from Latin America and Caribbean nations
His Excellency CHUM Sounry meets with Ambassador of Chile to China
On 21 August 2025, during the 10th FEALAC Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Ulaanbaatar, Mongolia, His Excellency CHUM Sounry, Secretary of State and Head of Delegation of Cambodia, held a pull-aside meeting with His Excellency Pablo Arriarian, Ambassador of Chile to China and Head of the Chilean Delegation
During the discussion, both sides highlighted the long-standing relations and friendship between Cambodia and Chile over the past three decades, marked by cooperation in trade, tourism, and political engagement
They recalled the consultation mechanism established through the Memorandum of Understanding signed earlier this year, and expressed the shared interest in convening the first round of consultations in 2026
An Inter-Ministerial Meeting to prepare for the upcoming 13th Cambodia-Japan Human Rights Dialogue
The meeting was attended by representatives from the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Justice, the Ministry of Information, the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, and the National Election Committee
His Excellency CHUM Sounry pays a courtesy call on Minister of Foreign Affairs of Mongolia
On 22 August 2025, on the margins of the 10th FEALAC Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Ulaanbaatar, His Excellency CHUM Sounry, Secretary of State and High Representative of Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, paid a courtesy call on Her Excellency Battsetseg Batmunkh, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Mongolia and co-Chair of the meeting
Her Excellency conveyed warm regards to Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn and expressed hope for a possible meeting between the two Foreign Ministers at the 80th UN General Assembly in New York
His Excellency Sounry commended Mongolia for successfully hosting the meeting with the Dominican Republic, resulting in the adoption of the Ulaanbaatar Declaration, which charts a vision for stronger interregional partnership and cooperation
He reaffirmed Cambodia’s commitment to expanding cooperation in trade, investment, education, tourism, and political dialogue
The two heads of delegation shared the view to convene the 2nd Bilateral Consultation between their Ministries of Foreign Affairs in Mongolia in 2026 and to hold it regularly every two years
They also discussed boosting tourism, including promoting Buddhist visitors to Cambodia and explored opportunities for broader ASEAN cooperation
His Excellency Dr. KHY Sovanratana has a cordial meeting with 17 Cambodian students
KHY Sovanratana, Secretary of State and Representative of His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a cordial meeting with 17 Cambodian students who have been awarded scholarships to pursue their studies in China
His Excellency Nong Sakal briefs diplomats on the latest developments in the Cambodia-Thailand border situation
On the morning of 26 August 2025, at the Ministry, His Excellency Nong Sakal, Under Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, held a briefing session on the latest developments in the Cambodia-Thailand border situation for the diplomatic corps from European countries, including the United Kingdom, Türkiye, the Russian Federation, Hungary, and the Czech Republic
His Excellency Nong Sakal underlined the importance of upholding peace and the Royal Government of Cambodia's strong commitment to the implementation of the ceasefire agreement in order to bring an end to the border dispute with Thailand and to return the situation to normalcy as soon as possible
On the morning of 27 August 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a meeting with His Excellency SUZUKI Hideo, Ambassador for Mekong Cooperation of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Japan, at the Ministry
On the morning of 27 August 2025, His Excellency PHIN Vicheawadhana, Under-Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received Her Excellency Milena Caridad Zaldivar Piedra, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Republic of Cuba to the Kingdom of Cambodia, at the Ministry
Both sides highlighted the enduring friendship between Cambodia and Cuba, noting that 2025 marks the 65th anniversary of their diplomatic relations
The meeting also touched on the expansion of bilateral cooperation, particularly the continued functioning of the Royal Embassy of Cambodia in Cuba and the Embassy of the Republic of Cuba in Cambodia, in line with the Reciprocal Exemption Agreement between the two Governments
Sun Sovanna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and Cambodia’s National Correspondent to the International Organization of la Francophonie (OIF), held a working meeting with His Excellency Mr
Dang Hoang Giang, Vice Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Socialist Republic of Viet Nam, in charge of International Organizations, at the headquarters of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs in Hanoi
The discussion focused on the progress of preparations for the 20th Francophonie Summit, to be held in Cambodia, and on the sharing of Viet Nam’s experience as host country of the 1997 Summit
