Her Excellency CHRING Botumrangsay pays courtesy call on Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Belarus
On 29 October 2025, Her Excellency CHRING Botumrangsay, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, paid a courtesy call on His Excellency Maxim Ryzhenkov, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Belarus, on the sidelines of the 3rd Minsk International Conference on Eurasian Security in Minsk
During the meeting, both sides reaffirmed their commitment to strengthening bilateral cooperation, particularly in promoting trade and investment opportunities
They also underscored the importance of the Bilateral Consultations between the two Foreign Ministries and expressed their readiness to hold the next round of Bilateral Consultations at the end of 2025 in Phnom Penh
Her Excellency Chring Botumrangsay visits the Belarus Tractor Works Factory
On the morning of 30 October 2025, Her Excellency Chring Botumrangsay, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, visited the Belarus Tractor Works Factory to explore opportunities for enhancing cooperation in the agro-industrial sector
She encouraged the Belarusian side to further invest in Cambodia to help increase production and create more job opportunities for the Cambodian people
