NAGASE Kensuke, Minister and Deputy Chief of Mission of the Embassy of Japan, at the Ministry
His Excellency KUNG Phoak holds a bilateral meeting with Ms. Bridget Collier, Deputy Head of Mission of the Australia Embassy to Cambodia
On the morning of 3 November 2025, His Excellency KUNG Phoak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and ASEAN SOM Leader of Cambodia, held a bilateral meeting with Ms
Bridget Collier, Deputy Head of Mission of the Australia Embassy to Cambodia, at the Ministry
Meeting between Deputy Prime Minister and the U.S. Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs
On the morning of 4 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, held a meeting with His Excellency Michael George DeSombre, U
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn conducts an inspection visit to locations designated for organizing the 20th Francophonie Summit
On 4-5 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, accompanied by the Ministry’s leaders and officials, conducted an inspection visit to locations designated for organizing the 20th Francophonie Summit to be held in 2026 in Cambodia
Handing over a house to the family of a military hero who sacrificed his life during Cambodia–Thailand border conflict
On the morning of 7 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, graciously handed over a house to the family of a military hero who sacrificed his life during the five-day Cambodia–Thailand border conflict
This ceremony was held in Trapeang Trach Village, Damnak Ampil Commune, Ang Snuol District, Kandal Province
Diplomatic Briefing for the Diplomatic Corps accredited to the Kingdom of Cambodia on the implementation of the Kuala Lumpur Joint Declaration on Peace, Cooperation and Prosperity
On the morning of 8 November 2025, at the Ministry, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, convened a diplomatic briefing for the Diplomatic Corps accredited to the Kingdom of Cambodia
The Deputy Prime Minister provided an update on the implementation of the Kuala Lumpur Joint Declaration on Peace, Cooperation and Prosperity, signed on 26 October 2025, which serves as a basis for rebuilding trust, peace and cooperation between Cambodia and Thailand
His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister outlined some priority areas agreed under the Joint Declaration and emphasized Cambodia’s faithful implementation of its commitments and readiness to work in close coordination with Thailand for the common interest of the two countries and peoples
Her Excellency Chring Botumrangsay attends the 4th Meeting of the Joint Economic Commission between Cambodia and Türkiye
On 4 November 2025, Her Excellency Chring Botumrangsay, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, attended the 4th Meeting of the Joint Economic Commission between Cambodia and Türkiye, co-chaired by Her Excellency Cham Nimul, Minister of Commerce of Cambodia, and His Excellency İbrahim Yumaklı, Minister of Agriculture and Forestry of the Republic of Türkiye, in Ankara, Türkiye
Both sides signed the joint agreed minute to enhance bilateral cooperation across key sectors and sub-sectors such as trade, agriculture, civil aviation, transport, education, health, investment, industry, tourism, halal cooperation, science and technology, water resources, labor and social security, mining and energy, and women’s empowerment, as well as other related fields with the aim of further strengthening our partnership and promoting mutual benefits for both countries
Her Excellency EAT Sophea leads the Ministry’s delegation to lay wreathes at the Independence Monument
Celebrating of the 72nd Anniversary of National Independence Day and the 72nd Anniversary of the Establishment of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces
On the morning of 9 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, led a delegation of the Ministry to attend the celebration of the 72nd Anniversary of National Independence Day and the 72nd Anniversary of the Establishment of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, highly presided over by His Majesty Preah Bat Samdech Preah Baromneath Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, at the Independence Monument
Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn chairs the third meeting of the National Organizing Committee for the 20th Francophonie Summit
On the morning of 10 November 2025 at the Ministry, His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, chaired the third meeting of the National Organizing Committee (NOC) for the 20th Francophonie Summit, which Cambodia will host in 2026
On the morning of 7 November 2025, at the Ministry, Her Excellency Phen Savny, Under Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received a courtesy call from Her Excellency Ivana Golubović-Duboka, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Republic of Serbia to Cambodia, with residence in Jakarta, after she had presented the Letters of Credence to His Majesty Preah Bat Samdech Preah Boromneath NORODOM Sihamoni, King of Cambodia
Both sides exchanged views on ways forward to further promote bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and Serbia, as well as continued support for each other at international fora
His Excellency NONG Sakal receives courtesy call by His Excellency Michel PARYS, Ambassador of Belgium to Cambodia
On the morning of 10 November 2025, His Excellency NONG Sakal, Under-Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, received a courtesy call by His Excellency Michel PARYS, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Kingdom of Belgium to the Kingdom of Cambodia, with residence in Bangkok, at the Ministry
They reaffirmed their shared commitment to further strengthening the bonds of friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and Belgium to an even higher level
The two sides also discussed general information regarding the upcoming Francophonie Summit, which will be held in Cambodia in 2026, during which a high-level Belgian delegation is expected to participate
Working luncheon in honour of His Excellency Cho Hyun, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Korea
On 10 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, hosted a working luncheon in honour of His Excellency Cho Hyun, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Korea, during his visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia
During the meeting, both Ministers discussed the ways to further strengthen bilateral relations between the two countries through enhancing cooperation on various fields, including trade, investment, defence and security and development
Her Excellency PHEN Savny receives courtesy call by His Excellency Tibor Baloghdi, Ambassador of Hungary to Cambodia
MOU Signing Ceremony between the Foreign Ministries of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Islamic Republic of Pakistan
On the morning of 11 November 2025, His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, presided over the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding on Consultation and Cooperation between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Islamic Republic of Pakistan
On the occasion, both sides expressed satisfaction with the existing relations between the two countries, and emphasized the importance of holding regular meetings to further strengthen bilateral cooperation and to explore avenues for harnessing the untapped potential and economic opportunities of the two nations
His Excellency Nong Sakal receives a courtesy call from His Excellency Danny Annan, Ambassador of Denmark to Cambodia
On the morning of 12 November 2025, His Excellency Nong Sakal, Under-Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received a courtesy call from His Excellency Danny Annan, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Kingdom of Denmark to the Kingdom of Cambodia, with residence in Bangkok, at the Ministry
Both sides exchanged views on general matters concerning the strengthening of Cambodia–Denmark bilateral cooperation in the political and economic fields, the promotion of people-to-people connectivity and exchanges between the two countries, as well as regional and international issues, including the possibility of enhancing cooperation within multilateral frameworks
Both sides also noted with satisfaction the growth in the number of Danish tourists visiting Cambodia
On regional and international issue, His Excellency Nong Sakal also briefed the Danish Ambassador on the latest developments along the Cambodia–Thailand border, particularly regarding the implementation of the Joint Declaration signed by the Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Thailand on 26 October 2025 in Kuala Lumpur
Both sides exchanged views on the importance of holding the first Political Consultation as a means to establish a framework for future cooperation
His Excellency KUNG Phoak has a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Marcos dos Reis da Costa, Ambassador of Timor-Leste to Cambodia
On the morning of 13 November 2025, His Excellency KUNG Phoak, Secretary of State and ASEAN SOM Leader of Cambodia, had a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Marcos dos Reis da Costa, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Democratic Republic of Timor-Leste to the Kingdom of Cambodia, at the Ministry
During the meeting, both sides underscored their shared commitment to strengthening cooperation and exchanged views on further advancing collaborative efforts that contribute to promoting peace, security, and stability in the region
Her Excellency EAT Sophea briefs Diplomatic Corps and international organizations on the latest developments of the Cambodia-Thailand border clashes
Her Excellency TOUCH Sopharath attends the 9th Working Group Meeting of the Conference on the Cooperation among East Asian Countries for Palestinian Development
On the afternoon of 13 November 2025, Her Excellency TOUCH Sopharath, Under Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, attended the 9th Working Group Meeting of the Conference on the Cooperation among East Asian Countries for Palestinian Development (CEAPAD), held virtually
This meeting was chaired by Japan, with the participation of representatives from CEAPAD member states, observers and other international institutions
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn participates in the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie
On the evening of 16 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, led a delegation of the Ministry to participate in the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie, which will be held from 19 to 20 November 2025 in Kigali, Republic of Rwanda
On the morning of 17 November 2025, Her Excellency Eart Sophea, Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received His Excellency Wihelm Maximilian Donko, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Republic of Austria to the Kingdom of Cambodia, with residence in Bangkok, for a farewell call at the Ministry
Her Excellency the Acting Minister thanked Ambassador Donko for his contributions to strengthening Cambodia-Austria ties and expressed appreciation to Austria for supporting Cambodia in demining and human resources development
She exchanged views with the Austrian Ambassador on ways to further expand cooperation between Cambodia and Austria, both in bilateral and multilateral spheres
They also touched on promoting trade and investment between the two countries
Ambassador Donko applauded the progress achieved by Cambodia in recent years
On the morning of the same day, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, held a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Olivier Jean Patrick Nduhungirehe, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Republic of Rwanda
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister expressed his deep gratitude to the Rwandan Government for the warm hospitality, extended to Cambodian delegation during his official visit to the Republic of Rwanda and participation in the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie from 19-20 November 2025
During the meeting, both parties discussed and explored the ways to further enhance cooperation between the two countries in political, economic, and cultural fields
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister leads delegation to a Wreath Laying Ceremony at the Kigali Genocide Memorial
On the morning of 18 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister, PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation paid an official visit to the Republic of Rwanda
During the visit, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister led delegation to a Wreath Laying Ceremony at the Kigali Genocide Memorial
On the afternoon of the same day, His Excellency Olivier Jean Patrick Nduhungirehe, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Rwanda, hosted a luncheon in honor of His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and his delegation during the official visit to Rwanda
On the afternoon of 18 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, hold a bilateral Meeting with Her Excellency Louise MUSHIKIWABO, Secretary General of the International Organization of Francophonie (OIF) in Kigali, Rwanda
During the Meeting, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister and Her Excellency Secretary General discussed the preparation for the 20th Francophonie Summit to be held in 2026 in the Kingdom of Cambodia
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn pays a courtesy call on His Excellency Justin Nsengiyumva, Prime Minister of the Republic of Rwanda
On the afternoon of 18 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, paid a courtesy call on His Excellency Justin Nsengiyumva, Prime Minister of the Republic of Rwanda in Kigali
During that occasion, His Excellency Prime Minister warmly welcomed the official visit of His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister to Rwanda and highly valued the growing bilateral relation between Cambodia and Rwanda
He emphasized that the signing of Memorandum of Understanding on the Establishment of Bilateral Consultations between the two Foreign Ministries and Agreement on Visa Exemption for Holders of Diplomatic and Offical Passports will further strengthen the bilateral cooperation between the two countries
The Opening Ceremony of the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie
On the morning of 19 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation attended the Opening Ceremony of the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie, held from 19-20 November 2025 in Kigali, Rwanda
The plenary session of the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie
On the same day, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation attended the plenary session of the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie, held from 19-20 November 2025 in Kigali, Rwanda
On the occasion, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister delivered intervention on the follow-up commitment undertaken at the 19th Summit of Francophonie, 30 years after the Beijing Conference: Women’s Contribution in the Francophone countries as well as Multilateralism cooperation, administrative and financial issues
On the morning of 20 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a bilateral meeting with the Honorable Christopher Skeete, Minister of International Relations and Francophonie of Quebec on the margins of the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie, held from 19-20 November 2025 in Kigali, Rwanda
On the occasion, both sides discussed the strengthening of the cooperation between Cambodia and Quebec under the Francophonie Framework, particularly Cambodia, being a host of the 20th Francophonie Summit in 2026 in Cambodia
His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister anticipate to see Quebec's active role and support to ensure the successful preparation for the 20th Francophonie Summit
Her Excellency YENTIENG Puthirasmy attends the launch and workshop on “The Situation Analysis Report on Women, Peace and Security in Cambodia”
On 20 November 2025, Her Excellency YENTIENG Puthirasmy, Secretary of State and Chair of the Gender Working Group of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, attended the launch and workshop on “The Situation Analysis Report on Women, Peace and Security in Cambodia”, presided over by Her Excellency Dr
ING Kantha Phavy, Minister of Women’s Affairs, held at the Cambodiana Hotel
The event aimed to raise awareness of the key findings from the situation analysis—focusing on evidence-based WPS priorities, challenges, and lessons learned—and to promote multi-stakeholder engagement to strengthen accountability and commitment toward developing the National Action Plan on Women, Peace and Security (NAP-WPS)
On that occasion, Her Excellency the Secretary of State highlighted the contributions of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation in promoting the Women, Peace and Security agenda through diplomacy, capacity-building, and international cooperation
On the morning of 19 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, had a bilateral discussion with His Excellency Maxime PRÉVOT, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs, European Affairs and Development Cooperation of the Kingdom of Belgium on the sidelines of the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie, held in Kigali, Rwanda
On the afternoon of the same day, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, held a bilateral talks with Her Excellency Eleonore Caroit, Minister Delegate to the Minister for Europe and Foreign Affairs, in charge of Francophonie, International Partnerships, and French Citizens Abroad in Kigali, Rwanda
During the talk, His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister briefed Her Excellency the Minister Delegate on the preparation for the 20th Francophonie Summit, scheduled to be convened in 2026 in Siem Reap, Kingdom of Cambodia
Her Excellency Minister Delegate expressed her intention to visit Cambodia in the near future to contribute to organising the 20th Francophonie Summit
On the morning of 20 November 2025, His Excellency KUNG Phoak, Secretary of State and ASEAN SOM Leader of Cambodia, had a bilateral meeting with His Excellency Mr
Christian DesRoches, Ambassador of Canada to the Kingdom of Cambodia, and Her Excellency Ambra Dickie, Ambassador of Canada to ASEAN, at the Ministry
The retreat session of the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie
On the morning of 20 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, attended the retreat session of the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie under the theme: "What ambitions for the OIF in the reshaping of the international landscape
On the afternoon of 20 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, held a bilateral discussion with His Excellency Ignazio Cassis, Head of the Federal Department of Foreign Affairs of the Swiss Confederation in Kigali, Rwanda
During the meeting, both Ministers highly valued the growing bilateral relations between the two countries and discussed the ways to further deepen the existing cooperation
His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister expressed gratitude for Switzerland’s development assistance, provided to Cambodia, especially in the areas of health, demining, culture, and local governance
Switzerland has expressed its strong support for Cambodia in assuming the host of the 20th Francophonie Summit in 2026 and looks forward to participating in this important event
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn attends the Handover Ceremony for the Presidency of the Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie
On the afternoon of the same day, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, attended the Handover Ceremony for the Presidency of the Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie (CMF) in Kigali, Rwanda
During the Ceremony, His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister extended sincere appreciation to the Republic of Rwanda, as a host, Republic of France as the President of the 46th CMF and Her Excellency Secretary General of OIF for their tireless efforts in effective fulfillment of the duties
On the occasion, His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister also announced Cambodia's priorities, being a President of the 47th CMF and a host of 20th Francophonie Summit in 2026 and expressed commitment to successfully organising the two events in Cambodia
Press Conference on the Outcomes of the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie (CMF)
On the afternoon of 20 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, attended a press conference alongwith Her Excellency Louise Mushikiwabo, Secretary General of the International Organization of la Francophonie (OIF), and Her Excellency Éléonore Caroit, Minister Delegate to the Minister for Europe and Foreign Affairs, in charge of Francophonie, International Partnerships, and French Nationals Abroad
This press conference provided an opportunity to present the outcomes of the 46th Ministerial Conference of La Francophonie (CMF), held from 19-20 November 2025 in Kigali and announce to the journalists the preparation for the 20th Francophonie Summit and the 47 CMF which will take place on 14, 15 and 16 November 2026 in Siem Reap, Kingdom of Cambodia
Her Excellency CHRING Botumrangsay visits Hungary to co-chair the Second Session of Political Bilateral Consultations
Her Excellency CHRING Botumrangsay, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia, paid a visit to Hungary on 21 November 2025, where she and His Excellency Péter Sztáray, State Secretary for Security Policy and Energy Security of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade of Hungary, co-chaired the Second Session of Political Bilateral Consultations between the two Foreign Ministries
Both sides reaffirmed their long-standing friendship and excellent cooperation, which have flourished across a wide range of shared interests, as reflected in the frequent and fruitful engagements between the high-level leaders of our two countries
The two sides also looked forward to the meaningful celebration of the 70th anniversary of the establishment of their diplomatic relations in 2026
They underscored the significance of the Political Consultations mechanism and high-level exchanges in advancing political, economic, and developmental cooperation
They also discussed regional and international issues of mutual concern, including updates on the Cambodia–Thailand border situation, and reiterated their commitment to promoting peace and stability
His Excellency TY Nitor and Her Excellency Ülkü Kocaefe deliver humanitarian assistance to displaced families
TY Nitor, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation (MFAIC), together with H
Ülkü Kocaefe, Ambassador of the Republic of Türkiye to Cambodia, delivered humanitarian assistance from the Government of Türkiye, amounting to USD 40,000
Her Excellency CHRING Botumrangsay and His Excellency Władysław T. Bartoszewski co-chair the Third Session of Bilateral Consultations between Foreign Ministries of Cambodia and Poland
Her Excellency CHRING Botumrangsay, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia, paid a visit to the Republic of Poland on 24 November 2025, during which she and His Excellency Władysław T
Bartoszewski, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Poland, co-chaired the Third Session of Bilateral Consultations between the two Foreign Ministries
They further emphasised the significant role of this bilateral dialogue as a mechanism to expand across-the-board-cooperation between Cambodia and Poland
The Co-Chairs reviewed with satisfaction the ongoing cooperation and identified further opportunities in key areas such as trade and investment, health, tourism, education, agriculture and agro-industry, culture, digitalization, people-to-people exchange, and parliamentary cooperation
At the same time, Her Excellency the Secretary of State expressed Cambodia’s deepest gratitude to the government of Poland’s continued support in human resource development through various scholarship programs
They also discussed the mutual supports for their respective candidatures for various positions in international organizations
On the afternoon of 24 November 2025, Her Excellency EAT Sophea, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received a courtesy call by Her Excellency Alona Fisher-Kamm, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the State of Israel to the Kingdom of Cambodia, with residence in Bangkok, at the Ministry
Her Excellency the Permanent Secretary of State exchanged views with Ambassador Alona Fisher-Kamm on ways to expand cooperation between Cambodia and Israel on agriculture, education, employment vocational training, tourism and innovation as well as and multilateral cooperation
Permanent Secretary of State EAT Sophea also briefed Ambassador Alona Fisher-Kamm on the latest developments along the Cambodia-Thailand border
His Excellency MEAS Kim Heng attends the regional workshop in Siem Reap
On 21 November 2025, His Excellency MEAS Kim Heng, Secretary of State and Chairman of the National Secretariat of Cambodia for the Mekong–Lancang Cooperation, attended the regional workshop in Siem Reap under the theme “Mekong–Lancang Tourism Sector Recovery and Resilience Action Plan 2026–2030
” The event was presided over by His Excellency HUOT Hak, Minister of Tourism, and His Excellency WANG Wenbin, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the People’s Republic of China to Cambodia
The workshop aimed to outline strategies aligned with current trends and regional priorities to attract more Chinese investors and tourists to Cambodia and the wider Mekong–Lancang region in 2026
Briefing to the Diplomatic Corps and International Organizations to Cambodia
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn pays an official visit to the Lao People's Democratic Republic
On the evening of 26 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, led a delegation of the Ministry to pay an official visit to the Lao People's Democratic Republic and co-chair the 15th Meeting of the Joint Commission for Bilateral Cooperation between Cambodia and the Lao PDR in Vientiane from 26 to 28 November 2025
Nong Sakal, Under Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, participated in the Annual Conference of the States Parties to the Chemical Weapons Convention, held in The Hague, the Netherlands
The conference was organized by the Organisation for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons (OPCW), with the participation of the Secretary-General of the Cambodia National Authority for Chemical Weapons and delegates
The opening ceremony of the consultative workshop on the draft internal public financial management guidelines of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation
Cambodian, Lao Foreign Ministers hold a bilateral meeting
On the morning of 27 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, held a bilateral Meeting with His Excellency Thongsavan PHOMVIHANE, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Lao People’s Democratic Republic in Vientiane, Lao PDR
Her Excellency EAT Sophea meets with Dr. HOSOYA Yuichi, Professor of International Politics at Keio University, Japan
On the morning of 27 November 2025, Her Excellency EAT Sophea, Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, met with Dr
HOSOYA Yuichi, Professor of International Politics at Keio University, Japan
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister pays a courtesy call on the Prime Minister of the Lao PDR
Later that same morning, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, paid a courtesy call on His Excellency Dr
Sonexay SIPHANDONE, Prime Minister of the Lao PDR in Vientiane, Lao PDR
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister was pleased with the strong bilateral ties in all areas including trade, investment, energy, connectivity, and transportation, which serve as a foundation for building a more stable and prosperous future for both nations
His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister pays a courtesy call on the President of Lao PDR and Secretary General of the Lao People’s Revolutionary Party
On the afternoon of 27 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, paid a courtesy call on His Excellency Thongloun SISOLITH, President of Lao PDR and Secretary General of the Lao People’s Revolutionary Party in Vientiane
His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister extended best wishes for the successful convening of the 12th LPR Party Congress, scheduled for early 2026, and reaffirmed Cambodia's commitment to working together to promote political, economic, socio-cultural cooperation and people-to-people exchanges
His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister also conveyed warmest regards and heartfelt congratulations from Samdech Techo HUN Sen, President of the Senate, and Samdech Thipadei HUN Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, on the auspicious occasion of the 50th Anniversary of the National Day of the Lao PDR in the upcoming December and looked forward to the meaningful commemoration of the 70th Anniversary of Cambodia-Laos diplomatic relations in 2026
The 15th Meeting of the Joint Commission for Bilateral Cooperation between Cambodia-Laos
On the morning of 27 November 2025, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, co-chaired the 15th Meeting of the Joint Commission for Bilateral Cooperation (JCBC) between Cambodia-Laos with His Excellency Thongsavan PHOMVIHANE, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Lao DPR in Vientiane, Lao PDR
In his opening remarks, His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister highly valued the importance of the growing bilateral ties between Cambodia and Laos that are bound together by years of solidarity and close cooperation
Both sides also reaffirmed their shared commitment to further strengthen this vital partnership for mutual benefit
The Meeting also reviewed the progress of the 14th JCBC Meeting between Cambodia-Laos and explored new areas to further deepen and broaden our cooperation
Towards the end of the Meeting, both sides attended the Signing Ceremony on the Agreed Minutes of the 15th JCBC Meeting
