Deputy Prime Minister holds phone call with EU High Representative Kaja Kallas
On the afternoon of 17 December 2025, His Excellency Prak Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia, held a telephone conversation with Her Excellency Kaja Kallas, High Representative of the European Union for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy and Vice-President of the European Commission
His Excellency Prak Sokhonn expressed Cambodia’s deep appreciation for the European Union’s support across various development sectors in Cambodia, as well as for its provision of humanitarian assistance to displaced people affected by the ongoing Cambodia–Thailand armed conflict
Her Excellency Kaja Kallas conveyed her condolences and sympathies for the civilian casualties and the hardships endured during this time of crisis
She reaffirmed the European Union’s readiness to provide further humanitarian assistance and to support peaceful solutions to the conflict through dialogue
His Excellency Prak Sokhonn emphasized Cambodia’s consistent commitment to the agreed ceasefire and the peaceful path outlined in the Kuala Lumpur Joint Declaration of 26 October 2025
He exchanged views with Her Excellency Kaja Kallas on the evolving situation and underscored the need to halt the fighting and restore peace along the Cambodia–Thailand border
Deputy Prime Minister PRAK Sokhonn receives credentials from Mr. Jürg Montani, Head of the ICRC Regional Delegation
