Montani briefed His Excellency on the ICRC’s recent visit to 18 Cambodian soldiers captured by Thai forces on 29 July 2025
Her Excellency CHRING Botumrangsay attends a cordial New Year’s Reception
On the afternoon of 17 December 2025, Her Excellency CHRING Botumrangsay, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, attended a cordial New Year’s Reception, graciously hosted by His Excellency Anatoly Borovik, Ambassador of the Russian Federation to the Kingdom of Cambodia, at his residence
In his welcoming remarks, His Excellency the Ambassador fondly reflected on the longstanding bonds of friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and Russia
On a note of sincere solidarity, he also expressed his heartfelt condolences and sympathy to the Cambodian people, particularly to the families affected by the Cambodia-Thailand border conflict
In this context, he conveyed his strong hope that Cambodia and Thailand would seek a durable and peaceful resolution through dialogue and diplomatic negotiation
