His Excellency Dr. Un Kheang receives courtesy call by recipients of the Australia Awards and Manaaki New Zealand Scholarships
Un Kheang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and High Representative of His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received a courtesy call at the Ministry from recipients of the Australia Awards and Manaaki New Zealand Scholarships for the 2026 academic year
During the meeting, His Excellency the Secretary of State congratulated the awardees, shared his personal experiences of studying, teaching, and living abroad, and reminded them of their responsibility as cultural ambassadors of Cambodia
Regarding the ongoing Cambodia–Thailand border situation, he urged the awardees to counter Thailand’s portrayal of itself as a victim and to expose its true intention of invading Cambodia, which has resulted in the loss of many Cambodian lives
He also highlighted the critical issue of brain drain and encouraged the awardees to return home upon completing their studies so they could apply their knowledge in service of the nation
