Remarks by H.E. Mr. PRAK Sokhonn, Senior Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation at the Signing Ceremony of the “Framework Arrangement concerning Loans From the Economic Development Cooperation Fund” and “Arrangement concerning a Loan From the Economic Development Cooperation Fund for Upgrading of National Road No. 48 Project” 31 January 2017.
This Framework Arrangement fund will be utilized to finance a number of priority projects relating to the fields of infrastructure, irrigation, health, rural road and sewerage system
It is important to note that this framework arrangement is well aligned with the priorities areas as laid out by the Royal Government of Cambodia within the Rectangular Strategy Phase III
As for the other arrangement, the project will be to renovate the national road no
I would also like to emphasize that the amount of this Framework Arrangement concerning EDCF loan for year 2016 through 2018 has increased more than twice from the previous Framework Arrangement (2013-2016), recorded at US$ 200 million
This increase testifies the continued strong commitment and support of the Government of the Republic of Korea to the Royal Government of Cambodia in its efforts for socio-economic development and improvement of the people’s well-being
May I recall that from 2001 to 2016, the Republic of Korea has provided EDCF loans to Cambodia with the amount of approximately 535 million USD for the implementation of 17 development projects
Taking this opportunity, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, I would like to express my sincere thanks to the Government and People of the Republic of Korea for their support to the development of Cambodia
